WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.977
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.277 --> 00:00:09.826
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.126 --> 00:00:17.121
Unit eighteen: Research Skills and Sources. Today you will find and judge reliable sources.

4
00:00:17.421 --> 00:00:20.119
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:24.416
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.239
Source.

7
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.505
Source means where information comes from.

8
00:00:30.117 --> 00:00:31.721
Check each source.

9
00:00:32.317 --> 00:00:35.132
Your turn. Say: Source.

10
00:00:37.967 --> 00:00:38.898
Source.

11
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:40.570
Reliable.

12
00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:43.780
Reliable means can be trusted.

13
00:00:44.383 --> 00:00:46.000
A reliable website.

14
00:00:46.583 --> 00:00:49.003
Your turn. Say: Reliable.

15
00:00:51.867 --> 00:00:52.845
Reliable.

16
00:00:53.583 --> 00:00:54.364
Journal.

17
00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.721
Journal means an academic magazine.

18
00:00:58.317 --> 00:00:59.759
Read a journal article.

19
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.037
Your turn. Say: Journal.

20
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:06.797
Journal.

21
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:08.505
Database.

22
00:01:09.517 --> 00:01:12.375
Database means an online collection of records.

23
00:01:12.983 --> 00:01:14.472
Search the database.

24
00:01:15.083 --> 00:01:18.049
Your turn. Say: Database.

25
00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:21.901
Database.

26
00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:23.349
Keyword.

27
00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.209
Keyword means a word used for searching.

28
00:01:27.817 --> 00:01:29.154
Choose good keywords.

29
00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:31.868
Your turn. Say: Keyword.

30
00:01:34.733 --> 00:01:35.502
Keyword.

31
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:37.414
Evaluate.

32
00:01:38.417 --> 00:01:40.765
Evaluate means to judge the value of.

33
00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:43.083
Evaluate each source.

34
00:01:43.683 --> 00:01:46.150
Your turn. Say: Evaluate.

35
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.117
Evaluate.

36
00:01:50.883 --> 00:01:51.606
Current.

37
00:01:52.617 --> 00:01:54.326
Current means up to date.

38
00:01:54.917 --> 00:01:56.254
Use current data.

39
00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.003
Your turn. Say: Current.

40
00:02:01.867 --> 00:02:02.740
Current.

41
00:02:03.483 --> 00:02:04.426
Bias.

42
00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:07.509
Bias means unfair preference.

43
00:02:08.117 --> 00:02:09.292
Look for bias.

44
00:02:09.883 --> 00:02:12.443
Your turn. Say: Bias.

45
00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.278
Bias.

46
00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:20.404
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.505
Visal, where do I find good sources?

48
00:02:24.617 --> 00:02:35.350
Use your university library, academic databases and journals. These sources are checked by experts, so they are more reliable than random websites.

49
00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:37.904
How do I judge a source?

50
00:02:39.017 --> 00:02:50.214
Ask who wrote it, why they wrote it, when it was published and what evidence it gives. Check for bias and compare it with other sources.

51
00:02:51.317 --> 00:02:52.805
How do I search well?

52
00:02:53.917 --> 00:03:03.384
Choose specific keywords, use synonyms and try different combinations. Note down every source you read so you can reference it later.

53
00:03:04.533 --> 00:03:06.301
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:10.856
Grammar focus: Questions for evaluating sources.

55
00:03:11.156 --> 00:03:12.424
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:13.117 --> 00:03:14.571
Who wrote this article?

57
00:03:15.483 --> 00:03:17.018
When was it published?

58
00:03:17.967 --> 00:03:24.047
Use who, why, when and what to question a source: Who wrote it? Why was it written? When was it published?

59
00:03:24.783 --> 00:03:28.875
Be careful! Don't say: Who wrote it is this article?

60
00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:32.926
Say: Who wrote this article?

61
00:03:33.226 --> 00:03:34.622
Do not repeat the verb.

62
00:03:35.433 --> 00:03:38.016
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:40.207
Choosing Sources.

64
00:03:40.507 --> 00:03:43.169
Sovann researches the topic of online learning.

65
00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:47.200
She searches a database with specific keywords.

66
00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.803
She checks the author, the date and the evidence.

67
00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:54.473
She rejects a website that seems biased.

68
00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:58.093
She keeps a list of her reliable sources.

69
00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.271
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:04.117 --> 00:04:06.383
A reliable source can be blank.

71
00:04:06.683 --> 00:04:09.942
A, trusted. B, ignored. C, erased.

72
00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.314
The answer is A: trusted.

73
00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.496
A journal is an blank magazine.

74
00:04:18.796 --> 00:04:22.101
A, food. B, academic. C, comic.

75
00:04:25.667 --> 00:04:28.026
The answer is B: academic.

76
00:04:29.183 --> 00:04:30.777
Current means up to blank.

77
00:04:31.077 --> 00:04:34.057
A, night. B, size. C, date.

78
00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:39.344
The answer is C: date.

79
00:04:40.483 --> 00:04:42.692
Evaluate means to blank the value.

80
00:04:42.992 --> 00:04:46.192
A, judge. B, print. C, lose.

81
00:04:49.733 --> 00:04:51.744
The answer is A: judge.

82
00:04:52.883 --> 00:04:54.581
What does Sovann reject?

83
00:04:54.881 --> 00:04:59.219
A, a book. B, a biased website. C, a journal.

84
00:05:02.767 --> 00:05:05.289
The answer is B: a biased website.

85
00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:09.594
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.705
How do you choose reliable sources?

87
00:05:21.517 --> 00:05:23.017
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:23.317 --> 00:05:36.374
I search library databases and journals with specific keywords. I ask who wrote the source, when it was published and what evidence it gives. I reject sources that show bias.

89
00:05:36.674 --> 00:05:38.395
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:39.283 --> 00:05:44.060
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and questions for evaluating sources.

91
00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:49.904
Today's value is critical awareness. Use technology wisely, and always think for yourself.

92
00:05:50.204 --> 00:05:52.833
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:55.530
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

